  "id": "82",
  "name": "Office administrative, office support and other business support activities",
  "section": "O",
  "summary": "Business-support companies split three ways: outsourcers and call-centre operators, for whom AI is both delivery tooling (agent assist, voice bots, speech analytics) and the main threat to volumes, headcount and per-FTE pricing; credit bureaus and collectors, who build scoring, decisioning and identity products under FCRA and fair-lending rules; and event organisers riding AI-themed demand. Outsourcers also sell into AI through data annotation, model evaluation and content moderation; fraud themes are voice cloning, deepfakes and synthetic identities.",
